    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat oven to 400°F.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Roughly chop walnuts and bacon; place in a large bowl along with gnocchi and mushrooms. Drizzle with oil, sprinkle with seasoning, and stir to combine. Divide between two baking sheet pans and spread out in an even layer.",
      "secondary_message": "½ cup walnuts\n8 slice bacon\n2 (16 oz) pkg potato gnocchi\n2 (8 oz) pkg sliced white mushrooms\n2 tbsp extra virgin olive oil\n2 tbsp herb and garlic seasoning"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place baking sheets in the oven (it doesn't have to be fully heated) and roast, stirring halfway, until mushrooms are tender and bacon is cooked through, about 30 minutes. Remove from oven, sprinkle with Parmesan, and stir to combine.",
